 training material and conduct end user training sessions before or after going live.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Provide demonstrations, knowledge transfer, administrator guidance, and functional handover documentation.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Maintain accurate meeting outputs, action logs, decisions, and stakeholder approvals.</p><h3>Mandatory experience and knowledge</h3><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; At least 5 years of business-analysis experience, including at least 2 years on ServiceNow implementation projects.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Previous ServiceNow implementation experience in at least one proposal-scope domain: Policy, Compliance, Risk, Audit, BCM, SPM, Demand, Portfolio, Project/Program Management, or a closely related capability.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Proven experience producing BRDs, process maps, user stories, acceptance criteria, use cases, traceability matrices, and UAT test cases.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ability to facilitate workshops with business owners, subject-matter experts, technical teams, and senior stakeholders.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Understanding of data, integration, role, workflow, notification, report/dashboard, and non-functional requirement categories.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Strong analytical writing and the ability to separate confirmed scope from assumptions, recommendations, and open issues.</p><h3>Preferred experience</h3><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience across both GRC/IRM and SPM; deep experience in one with working exposure to the other is acceptable.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Knowledge of BPMN, BABOK, agile delivery, ServiceNow implementation methodology, and regulated-enterprise governance.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Experience with requirements tools such as Jira, Azure DevOps, ServiceNow Agile Development, Confluence, or equivalent.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Arabic language proficiency (spoken and written) is strongly preferred; professional English is required.</p><h3>Academic and professional certifications</h